From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:07:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: align kernel-managed GPU iovas of 64 KiB+ objects to
 64 KiB

On the Surface Duo (Adreno 640), plasmashell's render targets trigger a
recurring CCU READ TRANSLATION fault and hangcheck recovery. The faulting
iova is always 64 KiB aligned and lies just below a UBWC color buffer
whose flag buffer is only 4 KiB aligned (e.g. flag base 0x1066da000,
fault at 0x1066d0000 = the flag base rounded down to 64 KiB), i.e. in
unmapped space before the object.

Kernel-managed VMs allocate iovas with PAGE_SIZE alignment. The
downstream kgsl driver aligns allocations of 64 KiB and more to 64 KiB;
do the same so such fetches stay inside the object.

Written with AI assistance (Claude).

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_vma.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_vma.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_vma.c
index 3b9a7cd4b..3eafedeb4 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_vma.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_vma.c
@@ -382,9 +382,24 @@ msm_gem_vma_new(struct drm_gpuvm *gpuvm, struct drm_gem_object *obj,
 	if (vm->managed) {
 		BUG_ON(offset != 0);
 		BUG_ON(!obj);  /* NULL mappings not valid for kernel managed VM */
-		ret = drm_mm_insert_node_in_range(&vm->mm, &vma->node,
-						obj->size, PAGE_SIZE, 0,
-						range_start, range_end, 0);
+		/*
+		 * Adreno a6xx fetches UBWC flag data in 64 KiB-aligned blocks: a
+		 * render target whose flag buffer starts mid-block makes the CCU
+		 * read below the buffer (iova = flag base rounded down to 64 KiB)
+		 * and fault. The downstream kgsl driver aligns every allocation of
+		 * 64 KiB or more to 64 KiB; do the same where the range allows it.
+		 * Fixed-address ranges (e.g. the GMU icache at 0x4000) keep page
+		 * alignment.
+		 */
+		ret = -ENOSPC;
+		if (obj->size >= SZ_64K)
+			ret = drm_mm_insert_node_in_range(&vm->mm, &vma->node,
+							  obj->size, SZ_64K, 0,
+							  range_start, range_end, 0);
+		if (ret == -ENOSPC)
+			ret = drm_mm_insert_node_in_range(&vm->mm, &vma->node,
+							  obj->size, PAGE_SIZE, 0,
+							  range_start, range_end, 0);
 
 		if (ret)
 			goto err_free_vma;
